        "collapsible_tab_DKyEmt": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How it fits your stack - and when it doesn't",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<ul><li>Most NAD⁺ supplements give you a precursor and stop there. But making NAD⁺ is only the first of three jobs - skip the other two and you're paying to produce NAD⁺ your body loses or never turns into energy you feel.</li><li><strong>Produce</strong> - NR gives your cells the building block they turn into NAD⁺. Essential, but on its own it's one third of the job. It's where NMN and NR stop - and where MUTO starts.</li><li><strong>Protect</strong> - An enzyme (CD38) breaks NAD⁺ down almost as fast as you make it. Quercetin, Pterostilbene, Grapeseed and Turmeric slow that leak, so the NAD⁺ you produce actually sticks around.</li><li><strong>Put to Work</strong> - NAD⁺ in your blood isn't energy yet. CoQ10 and BioPerine® help your cells absorb it and turn it into energy you feel - not just a better number on a lab report.</li><li>Produce without Protect is a leaking tank. Produce without Put to Work is fuel you never burn. NR and NMN do one job. MUTO does all three.</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
